@startuml
title hAFL2 (kAFL-based Hypervisor Fuzzing) - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam ArrowColor #3B6EA5
skinparam NodeBorderColor #555555
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #555555
skinparam ArtifactBorderColor #555555

package "Operator Host (hAFL2 Host)" as HOST {
  component "Standalone Test Runner\nkAFL-Fuzzer/test.py\n(Python 3 + pytest)" as TestRunner
  component "hAFL2 Orchestrator\n(kAFL-based workflow controller)" as Orchestrator
  component "Linux Packaging & Launch Scripts (bash)" as Packaging
  component "Initrd Builder" as InitrdBuilder
  component "Shared Library Collector" as LibCollector

  artifact "initrd\n[target binary + required shared libraries]" as INITRD
  artifact "Mutation Payloads (bytes)\nEffector Map (bool[])" as MUTDATA
}

node "kAFL Hypervisor" as HYP

node "Linux Guest VM" as LINUX_GUEST {
  component "Target Binary" as TargetBin
  component "Embedded Forkserver\n(Translate kAFL hypercalls -> AFL-style guest I/O)" as Forkserver
  artifact "Coverage/Exec Feedback" as Coverage
}

node "Windows Child Partition VM" as CHILD_VM {
  component "loader.exe\n(Snapshot create/load + execute packet_sender.exe)" as Loader
  component "packet_sender.exe\n(Triggers packet-sending IOCTL)" as Sender
  component "Harness Driver" as Harness
  artifact "Fuzzing Payloads" as FuzzPayloads
  artifact "Windows Offset Config\n(build-specific)" as WinOffset
}

node "Windows Root Partition VM" as ROOT_VM {
  component "Hyper-V Networking Path\nVMSwitch (vmswitch.sys)" as VMSwitch
  component "Crash Monitoring Driver/Service" as CrashMon
}

' Control and data flows (Linux userspace workflow)
TestRunner -[#3B6EA5]-> Orchestrator : Run test suites (FR-001, NFR-001)
Orchestrator -[#3B6EA5]-> Packaging : Launch userspace fuzzing workflow (FR-002)
Packaging -[#3B6EA5]-> InitrdBuilder
LibCollector -[#3B6EA5]-> InitrdBuilder : Copy required shared libraries (FR-004)
InitrdBuilder -[#3B6EA5]-> INITRD : Build initrd (DR-001, DR-002)

Orchestrator -[#3B6EA5]-> HYP : Manage boot/monitor
INITRD ..[#888888]..> HYP : Boot with initrd (FR-002)
HYP -[#3B6EA5]-> LINUX_GUEST

Forkserver -[#3B6EA5]<-> HYP : kAFL hypercalls / AFL-style I/O (FR-003)
Forkserver -[#3B6EA5]-> TargetBin : Execute fuzz iterations
MUTDATA ..[#888888]..> Forkserver : Payload + optional effector map (DR-003, DR-004)
Coverage -[#3B6EA5]-> Orchestrator : Coverage/exec feedback (FR-003)

' Control and data flows (Windows Hyper-V workflow)
Orchestrator -[#3B6EA5]-> Loader : Prepare snapshot + execute (FR-005, NFR-004)
Loader -[#3B6EA5]-> Sender : Load and run packet_sender.exe (FR-005)
Sender -[#3B6EA5]-> Harness : IOCTL: trigger packet send (FR-005; Communication Interface)
FuzzPayloads ..[#888888]..> Harness : Fuzzing payloads (DR-006)

Harness -[#3B6EA5]-> VMSwitch : Fuzzing payload path via VMBus/netvsc (FR-006; Communication Interface)
CrashMon -[#C23B22]-> Orchestrator : Crash status/monitoring result (FR-007, DR-007)

' Notes and constraints
note right of TestRunner
FR-001: Execute random, deterministic, havoc tests
NFR-001: Tests via pytest and standalone script
NFR-002/NFR-003: Deterministic mutation integrity & Hamming distance
end note

note bottom of LibCollector
FR-004 / DR-002: Identify and copy required shared libraries
end note

note right of Forkserver
FR-003: Embedded forkserver translates kAFL hypercalls to AFL-style guest I/O
end note

note bottom of Sender
FR-005: packet_sender.exe triggers packet-sending IOCTL
C-002: Build via bash ./hAFL2/targets/windows_86_64/compile.sh
end note

note bottom of Loader
FR-005: loader.exe creates snapshot, loads, executes packet_sender.exe
NFR-005 / C-004: Supports build-specific Windows offset configuration
end note

note bottom of Harness
C-003: Harness and crash-monitoring drivers compiled with Visual Studio
C-005: Disable DSE from elevated prompt; restart child VM
C-006: Configure child VM only when powered off
end note

note bottom of ROOT_VM
FR-006: Root partition Hyper-V VMSwitch target path
FR-007: Crash monitoring returns results to hAFL2
end note

note "C-001: BSD 3-Clause license; honor subfile licenses (incl. AGPL-3.0-or-later for kAFL-derived files)" as LicenseNote
LicenseNote -[dashed]-> HOST

legend
  == Notation ==
  Solid arrow: control/interaction
  Dashed arrow: data/artifact transfer
  Blue: workflow/control
  Red: crash/monitoring feedback
endlegend
@enduml
